10
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,291
This module covers 5 topics.

11
00:00:49,291 --> 00:00:54,683
Historical explanation for adaptation — Darwinian evolution explains adaptation

12
00:00:54,683 --> 00:00:57,004
through descent with modification.

13
00:00:57,004 --> 00:01:02,738
Variation and heritability — Natural selection requires variation, heritability, and

14
00:01:02,738 --> 00:01:04,717
unequal reproductive success.

15
00:01:04,717 --> 00:01:10,041
Natural selection mechanism — Fitness means relative reproductive success in a

16
00:01:10,041 --> 00:01:11,611
particular environment.

17
00:01:11,611 --> 00:01:16,867
Evidence for common ancestry — Fossils, homology, biogeography, and molecular

18
00:01:16,867 --> 00:01:19,119
evidence support common ancestry.

19
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:24,648
Fitness as reproductive success — Evolution changes populations over generations,

20
00:01:24,648 --> 00:01:27,174
not individual organisms during life.

21
00:01:27,174 --> 00:01:32,020
Each topic builds on the one before it, forming a coherent explanation.

22
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:35,338
